I posted one comment, on #1084, and left all the other issues alone.

#1084 (cost estimates that read low): progress noted, kept open. This session's commit 3ac62098 rewrote the "error direction" rule in docs/src/features/cost-tracking.md. It now turns on what sets the price. If that input reaches yoyo (the date, the endpoint, the prompt size), the cost table models the price change. Only if it doesn't does the table fall back to the higher rate.

Both rows in #1084 depend on inputs yoyo can see. Prompt size sets the tier for the session total, and DeepSeek's off-peak rate depends on the time of day. So the rule now says to model both, rather than switching to the peak rate or calling them exceptions. Neither row is fixed yet, and the doc still says "Two places do not meet that yet", which is why the issue stays open. I also noted in the comment that src/format/cost.rs is at its 3640-line limit, so the fix for either row belongs in a sibling module like the new promo.rs.

